A in the normal kidney</article-title><source>Kidney Int.</source><volume>45</volume><year>1994</year><fpage>998</fpage><lpage>1005</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7516453</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Nguyenetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nguyen</surname><given-names>X.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wang</surname><given-names>M.H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Reddy</surname><given-names>K.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Falck</surname><given-names>J.R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schwartzman</surname><given-names>M.L.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Kinetic profile of the rat CYP4A isoformsarachidonic acid metabolism and isoform-specific inhibitors</article-title><source>Am. J. Physiol. Regulatory Physiol.</source><volume>276</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>R1691</fpage><lpage>R1700</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Oyekanetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oyekan</surname><given-names>A.O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Youseff</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Fulton</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Quilley</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>McGiff</surname><given-names>J.C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Renal cytochrome P450 omega-hydroxylase and epoxygenase activity are differentially modified by nitric oxide and sodium chloride</article-title><source>J. Clin. lnvest.</source><volume>104</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>1131</fpage><lpage>1137</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Riccardietal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Riccardi</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Hall</surname><given-names>A.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Chattopadhyay</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surnam